  "prompt": "`memor compression-worth` reports only input-side figures. Output tokens bill at roughly five times input, so a compressed prompt that leads the model to write a longer answer can cost money while the report still shows a saving. The ledger has stored `upstream_output_tokens` for months and nothing reads it. Make the report account for output tokens, and make it say `unmeasured` rather than zero when an arm has too little data to tell. The relevant tests are in tests/test_compression_worth.py.\n\nRun the tests to see the current failures, then change the source so they pass. Do not edit anything under tests/ \u2014 the test files are restored from git before grading, so changes there are discarded. Do not change unrelated behaviour."
